It's OK, but I prefer Escaliber or Grayswandir, both two
weaponed with a Katana.  With Grayswandir, you can even keep the
Katana when you need silver; but Escaliber is much, much easier
to get -- almost a sure thing for a Samuri if he wants it.
I've had Grayswandir and a Katana both charged up to +7.
That's a real killing machine, and you only have to worry about
special attacts.  (Or not paying attention to the fact your
satiated before eating:->.)

Of course, you'll also want something for ranged attacts -- for
those monsters you don't want to get close to (and only those).
Arrows are the lightest -- and a Samuri can also get to expert
with a bow -- but daggers have the advantage that you don't have
to change weapons to throw them effectively.

With regards to the quest: there's nothing in it that a wand of
death won't handle:-).  I wouldn't go on it without reflection,
and a wand of death, but with those two, and preferably magic
resistance as well, two weaponing a charged up Excalibor or
Grayswandir and a Katana, it's not a real problem.

